{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc 'keelson impact src/flask/ctx.py src/flask/app.py tests/test_appctx.py && keelson --help && rg -n -C 5 \"do_teardown|teardown_.*context|appcontext_tearing_down|request_tearing_down|teardown_request|teardown_appcontext\" src/flask tests'","aggregated_output":"Impact hints for src/flask/ctx.py, src/flask/app.py, tests/test_appctx.py\nMechanical hints only: importers by name, specs and rules by path and words. They do not prove the impact list is complete.\n\nCallers / importers (31):\n  CHANGES.rst\n  docs/api.rst\n  docs/cli.rst\n  docs/deploying/gunicorn.rst\n  docs/deploying/mod_wsgi.rst\n  docs/deploying/waitress.rst\n  docs/design.rst\n  docs/extensions.rst\n  docs/patterns/celery.rst\n  docs/patterns/methodoverrides.rst\n  docs/patterns/packages.rst\n  docs/patterns/streaming.rst\n  docs/quickstart.rst\n  examples/javascript/js_example/views.py\n  examples/javascript/tests/conftest.py\n  src/flask/__init__.py\n  src/flask/cli.py\n  src/flask/globals.py\n  src/flask/sansio/app.py\n  src/flask/sansio/blueprints.py\n  src/flask/sessions.py\n  src/flask/templating.py\n  src/flask/testing.py\n  tests/conftest.py\n  tests/test_apps/helloworld/wsgi.py\n  tests/test_basic.py\n  tests/test_blueprints.py\n  tests/test_cli.py\n  tests/test_instance_config.py\n  tests/test_templating.py\n  tests/test_testing.py\nSpecs that may be affected (0):\nRules that apply (0):\n\nStill to check by reading: other entry points (CLI, jobs, API routes), data constraints, permission rules, compatibility promises.\nkeelson 0.4.0 — verifiable checks and durable decisions for coding agents\n\nUsage: keelson <command> [options]\nNormal use: run `keelson init` once, then talk to your coding agent as usual.\n\nYour commands:\n  init [--<platform> ...] [--tools a,b] [--guide] [--profile lean|guided] [--lang en|zh] [--no-hooks] [--vendor] [--dry-run]\n      Set up the minimal .keelson/ control plane and host discovery. Project artifacts grow only when the work needs them\n  status [--json]\n      Work, verification, and release status per change; slices, open questions, conflicts, handoffs\n  doctor [--session] [--json]\n      Diagnose the install: versions, hooks, config migration, validation, stale evidence, conflicts\n  update [--vendor] [--dry-run]\n      Refresh owned host shims and configuration; --vendor opts into copied guidance\n  platforms [--json]\n      List supported coding tools, their file locations, and which are installed or configured\n  uninstall [--purge]\n      Remove generated surfaces; keep .keelson/ unless --purge\n\nAgent workflow:\n  ask <add|frontier|list|settle|assume|reject|reopen> [id] [--change name] [--json]\n      Persist decisions and show up to three ready owner questions\n  context [--paths a/,b/**] [--json]\n      Print INTENT, ROADMAP, NOW, active changes, existing references, and the rules matching the given paths\n  impact <file> [file...] [--json]\n      Mechanical impact hints: importers, specs and rules that may be affected, active changes that overlap\n  focus [change] [--auto|--clear] [--json]\n      Bind this AI session to one active change without changing the change lifecycle\n  new <name> [--tier quick|spec] [--capability a,b] [--touches globs] [--depends change] [--worktree]\n      Scaffold a change directory (owner, branch, delta base recorded)\n  check [cmd...] [--record [claim]] [--change name] [--trust] [--timeout ms] [--quiet] [--json]\n      Run the project checks, save evidence, print or record a Verify entry with the worktree fingerprint\n  handoff [name] [--by who]\n      Create or re-stamp handoff.md for a change (at, updated, by)\n  validate [--json]\n      Check .keelson/ structure, specs, changes, ledgers; non-zero on errors\n  land [name] [--now \"<text>\"] [--confirm-assumptions] [--accept-drift] [--keep] [--force --reason \"<why>\"] [--dry-run]\n      Merge delta specs, fold decisions, remove or archive the change; refuses on stale or missing evidence\n  cancel <name> [--reason \"<why>\"]\n      Archive a change as cancelled without merging anything\n\nMaintenance / advanced:\n  guide [reference]\n      Read the installed workflow or one reference on demand\n  attest [change] [--json]\n      Export structured evidence and its local trust status\n  retro [--json]\n      Metrics from ledgers plus suggestions to prune guidance or add rules\n  models [--detect] [--refresh] [--resolve <tier>] [rank <alias> <tier>] [--platform <id>]\n      Resolve effort tiers to model aliases for this platform\n  ablate [--dry-run]\n      Temporarily remove every Keelson surface for an A/B comparison\n  restore [--force] [--dry-run]\n      Restore an ablated project byte-for-byte\n\nDocs: https://github.com/Atingaii/keelson/tree/main/docs\n/bin/bash: line 1: rg: command not found\n","exit_code":127,"status":"failed"}}
